WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.700
You might not recognize British actor and
comedian Simon Pegg these days.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.950
Apparently, he's been hitting the gym hard
the last several months in preparation for

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:13.980
his role in the upcoming indie drama Inheritance
— and he recently revealed a dramatic new

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.480
change to his appearance.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.920
Here's how he pulled it off.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.940
"So, what's the plan?”

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:22.620
… Right."

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.500
According to Pegg's trainer, the process of
getting him in shape for his new film took

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.520
six months.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.240
Consistency is key when it comes to reaching
fitness goals, and although to fans it might

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:37.120
seem like Pegg's transformation happened overnight,
the change actually took day after day of

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.660
putting in the work and doing the small things
right.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.440
Pegg's strong fitness base certainly helped,
too.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.840
Pegg has been working with trainer Nick Lower
for several years, so when he started his

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.900
Inheritance workout program, his body was
prepared.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.740
He had a good strength base built up, he was
used to disciplining himself, and he was familiar

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.660
with the process of working with a trainer
toward an end goal.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.420
That helped him reach his current level of
fitness after six months of work.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.140
Part of Pegg's training program was running
37 miles on the trails every week.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:11.480
Running is a good way to lose weight and get
healthy, but trail running might be even better

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.620
— according to the website Core Running,
it's a good functional workout because the

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.740
uneven terrain improves your balance.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.390
In other words, just going for a jog on flat
ground will tone your leg muscles and improve

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.840
your cardiovascular health, but it might not
get you in shape for other activities.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.520
Trail running can help you and your body be
ready for anything maybe even doing stunts

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.580
on a film set.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.160
And if muscle definition is your main goal,
trail running doesn't exclude that either:

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.659
Running downhill puts four to five times your
body weight on your legs, so it increases

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.780
your strength by leaps and bounds.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.800
Thanks to his weekly trail runs, not only
do Pegg's muscles look good now, but he's

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.740
also probably fast, agile, and ready for action.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.020
Pegg's workouts included a mix of strength
work, circuits, and core conditioning.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:00.420
Circuit training is a high-intensity type
of workout where you cycle through strength

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:05.200
and endurance moves, and it works because
it combines cardio and resistance training,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.740
helping burn fat, build muscle, and increase
overall endurance.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:13.760
Pegg's trainer had him doing circuit workouts
years ago when Pegg was preparing for Mission:

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.260
Impossible.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.360
In one video, Pegg referred to circuit training
as "Torture Tuesday."

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:24.360
Pegg would perform each planned exercise for
30 seconds, rest for 15 seconds, and then

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.160
do it again, until he'd completed the entire
workout three times.

00:02:28.569 --> 00:02:33.360
There's no word on the exact contents of Pegg's
circuits for Inheritance, but it was probably

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.900
doing something pretty similar.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.540
And it's not difficult to tell that Pegg focused
on strength work and core conditioning, too.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.520
According to trainer Nick Lower, Inheritance
required Pegg to be "very lean" and to have

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:49.540
a "specific body shape," and it seems like
Pegg ticked most of the boxes here as he worked

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.040
out.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.860
He did plenty of strength training and resistance
work, he followed a good nutrition program,

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:59.030
and it's evident from Lower's careful statistics
about Pegg's journey that he kept careful

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.700
track of Pegg's workouts.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.620
After all, recording the journey is the best
way to enjoy the end result.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.500
Maintaining a positive attitude during exercise
is important, but it isn't always easy.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.520
Pegg did admit to "occasional mild grumpiness"
on Twitter, but with the kind of grueling

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.870
workout schedule he followed, who wouldn't
have their ups and downs?

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.620
"It's entirely possible to be relaxed and
extremely uneasy at the same time.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:23.340
“No it’s not.”

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.620
“You do it all the time!”

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:25.240
“No I don’t.”

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.000
“Yes you do."

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.180
This does bring up an interesting point about
how important mindset is when it comes to

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:30.680
fitness.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.740
An Elite Daily article cites a scientific
study suggesting that positive thinking can

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.880
actually have a tangible impact on your workout
results.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.370
So while Pegg might have been grumpy about
the occasional early-morning trail run or

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:48.260
punishing "Torture Tuesday" circuit, we're
guessing that most of the time, he kept smiling.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.940
He might not have made as much progress if
he hadn't.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.420
Eating clean is another area where Pegg has
extensive experience.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.620
While preparing for Mission: Impossible, Pegg
followed a strict diet program with the help

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.360
of Tom Cruise's personal chef.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:05.120
How did Pegg's Inheritance diet compare to
his Mission: Impossible meals?

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:09.540
We can't say for sure, because his fitness
goals for this latest film are different.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:13.980
But when it comes to getting lean, nutrition
is half the battle, and Pegg certainly put

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.360
in his time in the kitchen as well as the
gym.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.760
Pegg has encouraging words coming in from
all sides.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.760
Each day in the gym, his trainer helps motivate
him and get him into action.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.680
His mom is one of his biggest supporters,
too on Lower's Instagram photo, she commented:

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.099
"Amazing Nick so proud of Simon and you for
the plan and support."

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.000
His fans are definitely on board, too.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.480
When Lower posted the photo of Pegg's transformation,
his notifications were flooded with good vibes.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.120
Much like the power of positive thinking,
support from the people around you is instrumental

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:48.120
in reaching any goal, fitness-related or otherwise.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.040
With Pegg's recent transformation, he's definitely
feeling the love.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.060
We can't wait to see the true fruits of his
labor when Inheritance arrives.

